  title="ISO 20000 Certification | Eurocert Asia"
  description="Explore iso 20000 certification with Eurocert Asia, including requirements, audit or assessment stages, documentation, certification support."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.eurocert.asia/management-system/iso-20000/"
  ogImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_webp,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367859/eurocert/Untitled_design_19_.png.webp"
  keywords="Eurocert Asia,Eurocert Asia,ISO certification,CE marking,food safety certification,FSSC 22000,BRCGS,GFSI,social audits,Sedex,SMETA,SA8000,inspection services,certification body,India,management systems,ISO 9001,ISO 14001,ISO 45001"
>
<style is:global>@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:900;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Brands";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-brands-400.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-regular-400.woff2) format('woff2')}</style>
<section class="relative min-h-[55vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[#030a16]"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_webp,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782368193/eurocert/m13.png.webp" class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-30" alt="ISO 20000 IT Service Management"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#030a16]/70 via-[#030a16]/40 to-[#030a16]"></div></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10 text-center py-20"><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-eurogold-400/30 bg-eurogold-400/5 mb-6"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400 animate-pulse"></span><span class="heading-font text-[10px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-bold">IT service management standard</span></div><h1 class="heading-font text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-3 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,168,67,0.3)">ISO 20000  -  IT Service Management</h1><p class="text-white/90 text-sm md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Framework for establishing, implementing, and continually improving a service management system.</p></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 items-start"><div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-6"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Standard Overview</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">ISO 20000  -  <span class="text-euro-600">IT Service Management</span></h2></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">To assess applicability, define organizational boundaries, the standard edition, services or activities, locations and intended assurance route before setting an audit scope.</p><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/40"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-info-circle text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">What is ISO 20000?</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">ISO/IEC 20000-1 specifies requirements for a service management system (SMS). It helps an organisation establish, operate, maintain and improve controlled processes for services within a defined scope. The service provider may be an internal IT function or an external provider. Certification addresses the system and stated services, not the technical quality of every product or a guarantee of availability.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-2 relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-slate-100 h-[320px] md:h-[400px] group"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_webp,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782368193/eurocert/m13.png.webp" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-105" alt="ISO 20000 IT Service Management"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900/20 via-transparent to-transparent"></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Discuss the standard, service scope and applicable audit criteria for your organisation.</p><div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#030a16] bg-eurogold-400 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-eurogold-300 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-eurogold-400/20" href="/contact/">Get Started <i class="fas fa-arrow-right text-[9px]"></i></a><a href="tel:+919316012883" onclick="return gtag_report_conversion('tel:+919316012883');" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white border border-white/15 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all"><i class="fas fa-phone text-[9px]"></i> Call Us Now</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white" aria-labelledby="standard-details"><div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl space-y-8"><h2 id="standard-details" class="heading-font text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Applying ISO/IEC 20000-1 IT service management in practice</h2><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Who should consider it?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">IT departments, cloud and managed-service providers, data-centre operators, telecommunications teams, software support organisations and shared-service functions may use ISO/IEC 20000-1. It can also apply to non-IT services when they fall within the SMS scope. Define service customers, boundaries, sites, people, suppliers, components and interfaces carefully. Where several providers contribute, the organisation should control interfaces that affect its in-scope service-management system.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Key requirements</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed"><li>Understand organizational context, interested parties, service requirements and SMS boundaries; assign leadership, policy, roles and measurable objectives.</li><li>Plan and control the service portfolio and lifecycle, including design, transition, delivery and improvement, with documented requirements and acceptance criteria.</li><li>Operate processes for incidents and service requests, problems, changes, releases, configuration, assets, availability, capacity and continuity as applicable.</li><li>Manage service-level agreements, service reporting, supplier relationships, information-security interfaces and business relationships so commitments and dependencies are controlled.</li><li>Monitor performance, keep records, conduct internal audits and management reviews, address nonconformities and improve using service data and customer feedback.</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Certification and audit lifecycle</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Agree the scope and assessment criteria first. Stage 1 checks SMS boundaries, service catalogue, documented processes, relevant sites and readiness, and may identify issues to address before stage 2. Stage 2 evaluates implementation and effectiveness by sampling service records, incidents, changes, releases, supplier controls, performance reports and staff practice. Findings must be handled under the certification scheme before an impartial decision. Surveillance audits occur at planned intervals, followed by recertification before the certificate cycle ends where certification is maintained. Audit time depends on services, sites, shifts, headcount, outsourcing, complexity and system maturity; planning must reflect those factors, not a generic promise.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Documents to prepare</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Prepare the SMS scope and service catalogue; context analysis; policy and objectives; process maps and responsibilities; service requirements and SLAs; incident, request, problem, change and release records; configuration and asset controls; availability, capacity and continuity plans; supplier agreements and reviews; service reports and customer feedback; competence and training; internal audits; management reviews; and corrective actions.</p></div><div><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">A useful scope statement distinguishes service-provider responsibilities from customer and supplier duties, identifies service locations and support arrangements, and explains how service-level targets are measured. Keep interfaces between service design, change control, operations and improvement visible in process maps. When a service depends on a supplier or another internal team, show how performance, incidents and changes are communicated and escalated. This makes audit sampling more representative of the service lifecycle rather than limited to policy documents.</p><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Frequently asked questions</h3><div class="space-y-4"><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Does ISO/IEC 20000-1 apply only to IT companies?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. It applies to organisations providing services and operating an SMS; scope is based on the managed services rather than the company label.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Can only one service be included?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">A defined scope may cover a subset of services when boundaries, interfaces, sites and responsibilities are clear and meet scheme requirements.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Is it the same as ITIL?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. ISO/IEC 20000-1 is a requirements standard for an auditable management system. ITIL is guidance and does not replace conformity to the standard.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">What happens during stage 2?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Auditors sample operational evidence such as service records, changes, incidents, suppliers and performance monitoring to evaluate SMS implementation.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">How is certification maintained?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Where granted, planned surveillance and a recertification assessment before the cycle ends are required under the applicable scheme.</p></article></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
